  "worked_solution": "The function is a composition of two functions, a logarithm function, and a cosine function.\n\nThe cosine is continuous at all points in its domain, and its domain consists of all real numbers. So, we focus on the logarithm function.\n\nLikewise, the logarithm function $\\operatorname{ln}\u2061(2x-8)$ is continuous at all points in its domain. To find its domain, we set the expression under the logarithm to be greater than zero:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}2x-8>0\\,\u27f9\\,x>4\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the domain of $f(x)$ is $(4,\\infty )$, and the function is continuous on this interval.",
